-- title:
--   True original ruin-clipped stopped physical Gaussian and negative marked-cell mixed energy under conull source Poisson domination
-- statement:
--   For the genuine original finite-activity spectrally negative Levy source, original ruin-clipped and upcross spatially-clipped stopping clocks and strict pre-ruin interior source mesh cells, the original stopped finite-mesh Gaussian and marked-jump square energy is integrable with uniform expected compact source budget, assuming the measurable marked-cell cardinal is dominated only almost everywhere by the original negative Poisson source count. Proved B72 supplies all true physical ruinclip interval/endpoint source bounds, Proved B70 provides bounded physical duration-square integrability, while B151 supplies the direct B150-based original preexit mixed energy estimate. This repairs B73 all-sample count domination and provides an original-source signed small-mark localisation component toward JB27. Publish only after B151 Proved.
-- source:
